{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/804805-buy-pdf-print-bind-legal","id":804805,"title":"Buy PDF, Print & Bind - Legal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-09T16:55:16-08:00","id":804805,"title":"Buy PDF, Print & Bind - Legal?","content":"Just a question - is it legal/allowed to buy, for example, the new Chronicles of Darkness core book on PDF, then put said PDF on a thumb drive, go down to Officeworks or similar and pay them to print and bind it? Provided we're talking just for personal use? Just worked out that provided I'm happy it's in B&amp;W (I am, usually) and don't care about the hard cover (I usually don't), it's a fair saving for me, but I'm still supporting the company.<br /> <br /> Just thinking it might be an option if I want to buy a particular book and either it is only available for PDF, or I can't afford the cost of the book and shipping, or I'm on a time-budget (I'm in Australia, and sometimes it can take up to a month for stuff to arrive). But I don't want to be screwing over WW/OPP/Paradox/whoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T17:55:04-08:00","id":804859,"title":"","content":"I'm ninety-five percent sure that's legal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T20:07:19-08:00","id":804947,"title":"","content":"It's kind of up to the PDF outlet, and the publisher. DTRPG used to have it listed in their FAQs, but I can't find it any more, that PDFs purchased through their site were legal to print yourself.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, for DTRPG, they leave it up to the publisher, since they can actually set a PDF file so it can't be printed. So if the print function for your PDF is on... it should be legal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T09:43:49-08:00","id":805305,"title":"","content":"I did it for the GMC update and was asked to provide a proof of purchase before printing begun","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T15:15:30-08:00","id":805527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/804805-buy-pdf-print-bind-legal?p=805305#post805305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did it for the GMC update and was asked to provide a proof of purchase before printing begun</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, well, that shouldn't be so hard, since DriveThru sends you that e-mail when you buy something. So I'd just make sure to have that cued up on my phone in case they ask.<br /> <br /> Thanks for that, guys <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T06:33:56-08:00","id":806029,"title":"","content":"Perfectly legal, but unless you're a bookbinding hobbyist, it's probably cheaper and more effective to just buy a hardcopy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:01:49-08:00","id":806576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/804805-buy-pdf-print-bind-legal?p=806029#post806029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfectly legal, but unless you're a bookbinding hobbyist, it's probably cheaper and more effective to just buy a hardcopy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not markedly. By my calculations, using the given prices on the Officeworks website, it'd cost maybe $35 to print and bind it, with PDFs going for about $20 - less if you wait until there's a special on.<br /> <br /> I checked how much it'd cost the buy a book on DriveThru, came out to $55.42, with shipping.<br /> <br /> Given that it can often take up to a month for books to arrive, and the unreliability of my post, not a terrible option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T18:39:42-08:00","id":806651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/804805-buy-pdf-print-bind-legal?p=806576#post806576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not markedly. By my calculations, using the given prices on the Officeworks website, it'd cost maybe $35 to print and bind it, with PDFs going for about $20 - less if you wait until there's a special on.<br /> <br /> I checked how much it'd cost the buy a book on DriveThru, came out to $55.42, with shipping.<br /> <br /> Given that it can often take up to a month for books to arrive, and the unreliability of my post, not a terrible option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did say probably. Obviously OOP books or books traveling around the world can drive up the price of a &quot;real&quot; copy. But the printed out copy is usually much lower quality unless you pay top dollar for the paper and ink, which drives the price up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T19:31:59-08:00","id":806681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/804805-buy-pdf-print-bind-legal?p=806651#post806651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did say probably. Obviously OOP books or books traveling around the world can drive up the price of a &quot;real&quot; copy. But the printed out copy is usually much lower quality unless you pay top dollar for the paper and ink, which drives the price up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was I unclear as to my purpose? My apologies, I thought I was.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/804805-buy-pdf-print-bind-legal#post804805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just worked out that <b>provided I'm happy it's in B&amp;W (I am, usually) and don't care about the hard cover (I usually don't)</b>, it's a fair saving for me, but I'm still supporting the company...<br /> <br /> Just thinking it might be an option if...I'm on a time-budget (I'm in Australia, and sometimes it can take up to a month for stuff to arrive)</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously the savings are not as great as I thought they would be, but the rest still is valid. I was just wondering if it <i>was</i> an option I could take without, not how I'm going to be buying 100% of my books from this moment forward.<br /> <br /> Not sure how I could have made that clearer, but obviously I could have. My apologies, I'll try harder in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}